<article class="env-lemma" id="0BZG">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0BZG">Lemma <span data-tag="0BZG">48.13.4</span>.</a> Let $f : X \to Y$ be a perfect proper morphism of Noetherian schemes. Let $g : Y' \to Y$ be a morphism with $Y'$ Noetherian. If $X$ and $Y'$ are tor independent over $Y$, then the base change map (<a href="/tag/0AA6" data-tag="0AA6">48.5.0.1</a>) is an isomorphism for all $K \in D_\mathit{QCoh}(\mathcal{O}_ Y)$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      By Lemma <a href="/tag/0AAA" data-tag="0AAA">48.13.2</a> formation of the functors $a$ and $a'$ commutes with restriction to opens of $Y$ and $Y'$. Hence we may assume $Y' \to Y$ is a morphism of affine schemes, see Remark <a href="/tag/0E9S" data-tag="0E9S">48.6.1</a>. In this case the statement follows from Lemma <a href="/tag/0AA8" data-tag="0AA8">48.6.2</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>